# Roles & Permissions

## Role Architecture

CampusOps uses two tiers of roles:

1. **Platform roles** — apply to the `campusops-platform` super organization only
2. **Organization roles** — scoped per school organization

All role codes, permission codes, and role definitions live in:
- `apps/api/src/permissions/constants/system-permissions.ts` — permission catalog
- `apps/api/src/permissions/constants/system-roles.ts` — role definitions

## Organization Roles (School-level)

| Role Code | Name | Primary Users |
|-----------|------|--------------|
| `SCHOOL_ADMIN` | School Admin | IT admin, school management |
| `PRINCIPAL` | Principal | Head of school |
| `TEACHER` | Teacher | Teaching staff |
| `RECEPTIONIST` | Receptionist | Front desk / reception |
| `MAINTENANCE_STAFF` | Maintenance Staff | Facility / maintenance team |
| `ACCOUNTANT` | Accountant | Finance/accounts team |
| `STAFF` | Staff (self-service) | General staff — self-service portal only |
| `STUDENT` | Student | Student self-service portal |
| `PARENT` | Parent | Parent portal for linked students |

## Role Scoping Rules

- `SCHOOL_ADMIN` sees all modules — full access
- `PRINCIPAL` sees operational dashboard, leave approvals, complaints, notices, events, reports — no staff management
- `TEACHER` has staff self-service (leave, attendance self-view), notices, events, complaints (create only)
- `RECEPTIONIST` sees visitors, notices, events, document generation (visitor pass)
- `MAINTENANCE_STAFF` sees complaints only (view + update assigned)
- `ACCOUNTANT` sees fees, assets, documents, approval participation, fee reports
- `STAFF` has self-service only: own dashboard, own leave, own attendance
- `STUDENT` has student self-service: own profile, own fees, certificate download, notices, events
- `PARENT` has the parent portal, notices, and linked students' transport

## Custom Roles & Admin-Edited Permissions

School admins manage roles at **Settings → Roles & permissions** (`/settings/roles`), backed by `RoleManagementService` (`apps/api/src/roles/role-management.service.ts`):

- `role.create` / `role.update` / `role.delete` (granted to `SCHOOL_ADMIN`)
- Custom roles get `isSystem = false` and a generated code `CUSTOM_<NAME>`; they can be renamed and deleted (only when no users or approval levels use them)
- Built-in roles (`isSystem = true`) cannot be renamed or deleted, but their permissions can be edited; editing sets `permissionsCustomizedAt`, and **the seed never re-syncs a customized role**. `POST /roles/:id/reset` restores the code definition
- `SCHOOL_ADMIN` permissions are locked to prevent lockout
- `platform.*` permissions can never be granted to an organization role; non-admin editors can only grant permissions they hold
- The permission picker groups the catalog via `apps/api/src/permissions/constants/permission-groups.ts` — add a group there when adding a new module prefix
- Because admins can customize built-in roles, ship new permissions for existing roles via a **SQL migration** (see `20261118120100_class_permissions`), not only by editing `system-roles.ts`
- Logic that checks role **codes** (Principal leave approval, Parent/Student portals) does not apply to custom roles — prefer permission checks in new code

## Frontend Navigation Filtering Rule

**Never show a sidebar nav item if the user does not have at least one required permission for that module.**

Each nav item in `AppShell` must declare its required permission(s).
The sidebar renders only items where `hasPermission(user.permissions, item.requiredPermission)` is true.

## Role Seeding

- Roles are seeded automatically when a new school organization is created (onboarding flow)
- A one-time migration script exists at `apps/api/scripts/seed-org-roles.ts` to seed roles for existing organizations
- New role definitions added to `ORGANIZATION_ROLE_DEFINITIONS` are automatically applied by re-running the seed script
- Never hardcode role IDs — always resolve by `organizationId + roleCode`

## Permission Naming Convention

Format: `resource.action`

Examples:
- `staff.view` `staff.create` `staff.update` `staff.deactivate`
- `leave.view` `leave.create` `leave.approve` `leave.reject`
- `student.self.view` `student.self.fee.view` `student.self.certificate.download`

Self-service permissions use `resource.self.action` pattern.

## Security Enforcement

- Role and permission checks happen on the **backend** — frontend filters are UX only
- Every API endpoint uses the `@RequirePermission('permission.code')` guard
- Never trust a client-supplied roleId or organizationId
- Assigning a role to a user requires `role.assign` permission
